btype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Key steps for a directly held account in a whole-fund conversion:**\n\n- **Read every notice.** Prospectus supplements, information statements or proxies, and transfer-agent letters set *your fund's* dates and default treatment. In a full conversion the mutual fund ceases to exist, unlike adding an ETF share class, where it continues.\n- **Open a brokerage account.** ETF shares generally can't sit at the transfer agent. Open a brokerage account (or IRA there for retirement money) and transfer in kind before the deadline.\n- **Know the default.** Missing the deadline may mean shares are parked in a restricted account until moved, or liquidated, which could be taxable.\n- **Expect trading changes.** You'll trade on an exchange through your broker at market prices, with bid-ask spreads. Automatic investment plans, exchanges and checkwriting typically end.\n- **Fractional shares.** These are usually paid out in cash, potentially taxable. Keep your cost-basis records.","ttft_ms":1389,"type":"result","duration_ms":3646,"uuid":"0ffc39de-e1d2-4946-8260-3e65d965a156","ttft_stream_ms":1277,"time_to_request_ms":53,"first_content_frame_ms":1277,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
